{"analysis":"Primary contrast: after-meta minus ordinary. 10000 crossed bootstrap draws over independent model draws and paired workload samples stratified by family; 95% interval. Conditional on one meta-development run, not uncertainty over repeated meta training. No optional stopping or replacing failures.","base":"14-job single-start nearest-neighbor scheduler, starting at job 0","costs":"Record calls, input/output tokens, wall time. Subscription dollar billing unknown. No equal-total-budget control; no claim that meta is more compute efficient.","created_at":"2026-11-12T04:14:09.935545+00:00","diagnostic":"If meta is rejected, additionally run 32 full inner native optimizations with the better training-scoring proposed instruction. Label as forced instruction diagnostic, not actual meta adoption.","final_policy":"Use the reopened ACTIVE improver after the native meta pass. If meta is rejected, retain the original instruction. Never force a proposed revision into the primary third arm.","final_samples_per_arm":32,"gate_version":3,"inner_minimum_effect":0.02,"limits":["Synthetic workload, not production throughput","Same model alias, not immutable weights","LLM optimization with deterministic non-LLM scoring and review","No LLM calls at scheduler inference time"],"meta_development_calls":73,"meta_minimum_effect":0.005,"model":"gpt-6-astra","model_call_limit":169,"model_concurrency":2,"model_timeout_seconds":600,"native_training_shadow_verification":"Each has two case batches of sixteen workloads; each final model draw runs full native selection, shadow, adoption and verification from the SAME original base.","outer_training_shadow_verification":"Each has eight independent complete native optimization runs, grouped into two batches of four; distinct model draws and evaluation workloads across the three stages.","provenance":{"checkout_revision":"c7cdd17e3594421120e719c0a85fd2d1d1e0e262","files_sha256":{"examples/adaptive_strategy.py":"81f2504e7810d479263e2f3bc5fa9